From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nf_flow_table: read final hardware stats before
 deleting an offloaded flow

With a counter-enabled hardware flowtable, conntrack accounting only sees
offloaded traffic through the periodic FLOW_CLS_STATS poll. The DESTROY
work deletes the hardware record without a last poll, so the packets and
bytes forwarded since the previous poll are lost. With patch 140 a TCP flow
is deleted at its first FIN, so every offloaded TCP connection loses its
tail (board .185, 2026-11-02: a 10 s iperf3 flow reported 5.62M packets to
conntrack while the silicon record had already counted 6.12M two seconds
before the end; UDP flows that age out were exact).

Run the stats work for the flow before the delete when the flowtable has
NF_FLOWTABLE_COUNTER set.

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
---
diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
index 1bd76c2..b05bf9d 100644
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -1066,6 +1066,13 @@ static void flow_offload_work_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 			NF_FLOW_TABLE_STAT_DEC_ATOMIC(net, count_wq_add);
 			break;
 		case FLOW_CLS_DESTROY:
+			/* Harvest the counters accrued since the last stats
+			 * poll before the hardware record is deleted, or the
+			 * tail of every offloaded flow is lost to conntrack
+			 * accounting (up to one gc interval per flow).
+			 */
+			if (offload->flowtable->flags & NF_FLOWTABLE_COUNTER)
+				flow_offload_work_stats(offload);
 			flow_offload_work_del(offload);
 			NF_FLOW_TABLE_STAT_DEC_ATOMIC(net, count_wq_del);
 			break;
